is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: spine_router_0_0
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the BGP control-plane on spine_router_0_0 (FRR/bgpd daemon) is down. Mechanism: when bgpd stops on spine_router_0_0, all its eBGP sessions to adjacent devices immediately transition to Active/Down, while dataplane links remain UP. The other nodes still have their alternate BGP sessions to spine_router_0_1, so traffic continues and hosts retain reachability, but the fabric loses its intended redundancy.

Localization and evidence:
- On spine_router_0_0, “show bgp summary” returns “bgpd is not running” and systemctl shows “frr.service … Active: inactive (dead)”, confirming the BGP daemon (and FRR supervision) isn’t running.
- netstat on spine_router_0_0 does not show bgpd’s vty port (2605)
